# Never let Git touch line endings.
#
# This project's correctness rests on byte-identical file writes (the writer is verified to
# reproduce unmodified sub-files byte-for-byte, and the test suite compares raw bytes). Files here
# were authored with mixed LF and CRLF endings, so any EOL normalization would both rewrite content
# on checkout and bury real changes in whitespace churn.
#
# "-text" disables all EOL conversion on every platform, for every file type. Content is stored and
# restored exactly as it is on disk. Diffs still work normally.
* -text
